 More information: [Build from source](https://github.com/LibreCAD/LibreCAD/wiki/Build-from-source)
 
+### Using an installed libdxfrw (CMake)
+
+LibreCAD builds its bundled codec by default. To use a separately installed,
+compatible libdxfrw CMake package instead:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build-system -DLIBRECAD_USE_SYSTEM_LIBDXFRW=ON \
+  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/path/to/libdxfrw/prefix -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF
+cmake --build build-system
+```
+
+If changing the prefix in an existing build directory, clear the cached
+`libdxfrw_DIR` value or configure a fresh build directory. The complete
+`BUILD_TESTS` suite currently requires bundled private codec headers. To run
+the focused public-header checks with an installed Catch2 v3 package (or the
+Catch2 submodule), configure the system build with
+`-DLIBRECAD_BUILD_SYSTEM_CODEC_TESTS=ON`, then run:
+
+```sh
+cmake --build build-system --target librecad_system_codec_tests
+ctest --test-dir build-system -R '^librecad_system_codec_' --output-on-failure
+```
+
+These focused checks do not qualify all formats or replace the complete suite.
+
 ### Plugin Installation
 
 CMake accepts `-DLIBRECAD_PLUGIN_INSTALL_DIR=lib/librecad/plugins` to override
